# Response headers for every route (#8). Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build
# output directory, which wrangler.toml points at ./public.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here, deliberately. A CSP is the header worth having on a screen
# that renders model output, and it is also the one that breaks a deployment in a way nobody
# notices until a recruiter cannot copy a pack. It needs its own ticket and its own smoke pass.
# The three below cost nothing and cannot break a working page.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
